Root cause and repro from draw.io desktop, where all printing broke after moving to 43 (jgraph/drawio-desktop#2476, jgraph/drawio-desktop#2484).

webContents.print(opts) fails with "Invalid printer settings" for any non-empty opts. print({}) works. Not Linux specific, we see it on Windows, macOS and Linux. Broken in 43.0.0 through 43.1.1 and on main as of 44.0.0-alpha.3. 42.x is fine.

Cause: Chromium moved UpdatePrintSettings() out of PrintViewManagerBase into the preview-only PrintViewManager. PrintViewManagerElectron now overrides it and rejects every request:

https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/v43.1.1/shell/browser/printing/print_view_manager_electron.cc#L119-L123

```cc
void PrintViewManagerElectron::UpdatePrintSettings(
    base::DictValue job_settings,
    UpdatePrintSettingsCallback callback) {
  std::move(callback).Run(nullptr);
}
```

In 42.x there is no override, so the working base class implementation handled it. Any print call that carries settings now fails before the system dialog opens.

Minimal repro:

```js
const { app, BrowserWindow } = require('electron')

app.whenReady().then(() => {
  const win = new BrowserWindow()
  win.loadURL('data:text/html,<h1>print test</h1>')
  win.webContents.once('did-finish-load', () => {
    win.webContents.print({ printBackground: true }, (ok, err) => {
      console.log(ok, err) // false 'Invalid printer settings' on 43, dialog opens on 42
    })
  })
})
```

Our workaround is to retry with print({}) when that error comes back, but then pageSize, scaleFactor and margins are all ignored. We have reverted to 42.7.0 for now. Happy to test a fix.
